From b45e04986ede76eafc42014aa42be2cb090f9096 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ztOS build <build@localhost>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 01:26:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media, regulator, clk: Galaxy S10 cameras from the S10e port

The camera stack of pulpoff/linux-beyond0lte (commit 47d26e62, "S10e:
cameras, ..."), GPL-2.0, on v7.2.0 + S10Plus_Linux:

- exynos9820-csis: CSIS v5.2 + WDMA capture (sensor -> D-PHY -> CSIS ->
  DMA -> DRAM, no ISP firmware, no secure calls)
- s5k3p9: one V4L2 driver for the S5K3P9, S5K3J1 and S5K2L4 with the
  stock tables; ak7375: the AK737x actuators
- s2mpb02/s2mpb03: the camera PMICs

and CMU_ISPPRE (0x17000000) in the S10Plus_Linux clock driver, which has
the PERIC1 camera I2C clocks already but not this block: the S10e block
in this driver's style (no auto clock gating, CLKS_NR_ naming), registered
with the other platform CMUs through exynos_arm64_register_cmu_pm().
